        id: "forgeweave:pickaxe"
    },
    what: "#993 (JC-D): an atomic_matter_alloy pickaxe carrying its own modifier, trait, stats and energy buffer, plus a block of Mekanism module state alongside them. What it pins is that Forgeweave's decode neither drops the foreign half nor lets it displace its own -- the same rule m8_affixed.snbt pins for Apotheosis. The module block sits under minecraft:custom_data rather than on Mekanism's real mekanism:module_container component type, for m8_affixed's own reason: Mekanism is compileOnly, its DataComponentTypes are not in a registry every unit test can reach, and ItemStack.CODEC refuses a component type it cannot resolve. Its keys mirror what Mekanism 10.7.19 stores -- one entry per installed module type, with its installed count and its enabled flag -- so the fixture pins Forgeweave's rule rather than Mekanism's serialization, which is Mekanism's to change. One of the three modules is switched off on purpose: Forgeweave must carry that through as faithfully as the two that are on."
}
